{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Before Ashley started a three-hour drive, her car's odometer reading was 29792, a palindrome. (A palindrome is a number that reads the same way from left to right as it does from right to left). At her destination, the odometer reading was another palindrome. If Ashley never exceeded the speed limit of 75 miles per hour, which of the following was her greatest possible average speed?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d9feddef79cba61b726ef2e2a98f96b2e3a68c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 33\\frac 13 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }53\\frac 13 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }66\\frac 23 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }70\\frac 13 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 74\\frac 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"452\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ashley could have traveled at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13ac2415aa770e4b46f508f28edf239c43ddf307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times 75 = 225$\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" /> miles.\n</p><p>Each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit palindrome is uniquely determined by its first three digits. The next palindromes are 29892, 29992, 30003, and 30103. We may note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec5e568f3c2bbe80d9287d54fe61f38b969869b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30103-29792 = 311 &gt; 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"215\" height=\"13\" />, so this number and all larger ones are too large.\n</p><p>On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae7625995c64c90e1f5e638954751c6b35e5f6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30003 - 29792 = 211 \\leq 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"15\" />, thus this is the number on the odometer, and the average speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d36c17ac2de6552e6d14055c5ad5a946681cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{211}3 = \\boxed{(D) 70 \\frac 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"128\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href